Date: Sun, 18 Oct 2026 10:26:48 +0000
Subject: [PATCH 1/5] fix(address): words with a dot that are not domains are
 searches, not addresses

"file.txt", "node.js", "setup.exe", "image.jpg" and "Dr.Who" opened https://<word>
and ended on a "couldn't find" page. A typed word is a site only when its last label is
a delegated top-level domain (or xn--, or a name private networks use: .local, .lan, .home).

KnownTopLevelDomains holds the 1287 Latin root-zone entries (npm tlds 1.261.0); the test
keeps the list sorted and unique. localhost and IP addresses are unchanged.

